Z||000000||fierobaby||06-27-2001||04:17 PM||||ok so my sunroof leaks woopty doo well the privious owner kept electrical tape on it but now the tape seems to have left goo! Yes GOO! I need something that won't ruin my paint... Nailpolish remover worked nicely on the windows and bumper...but on paint...ummm noooo any ideas and to clean my engine I was told to use No touch.... who makes it?<P>------------------<BR>1984 Sweet Candy Apple red Fiero sport coupe :-D<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by fierobaby (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||The Dealer||06-27-2001||04:48 PM||||there is a product called Kronar that works well.  It  is a prepping chemical used to clean un-painted and painted surfaces of all oils and residues, such as the goo... so it is ready for paint.  You can probably find this stuff at a body shop... I'm pretty sure Dupont makes it, but I don't remember, it has been a while since I have used it, my Dad has the stuff and I just drop by if I need to do painting, he worked in a body shop for a time.<P>The Dealer||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tina||06-27-2001||05:03 PM||||I would check at a bigger parts-store the next time your there.<BR>Seem to remember seeing something like that at Pep-Boys. Right there in the aisle where they sell the decals, stripes, and stuff.<P>Tina <BR>BTW Isn't it amazing what nailpolish remover can do,besides it's intended job?<BR>Say, did you use "acetone or non-acetone"?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
