Z||000008||stsmithgt||06-27-2001||07:12 PM||||I've also used <B>Goo Gone</B> to get the left over goo off my car when I removed my quarter windows.  It works well.  I don't think it's as harsh as <B>Goof Off</B>, but I was only  going by the smell.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> I used Goo Gone on strips of old Levi pants.  The material is a soft, absorbant and tough enough to get the goo off.  I went through a lot of it, but I have a lot of old Levis I can cut up too.  It worked a hell  of a lot better than the paper towel I tried.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg">   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||14
